(5666,1,0,'When time permits, we must speak at length.  For we have much to discuss.',12,0,100,1,0,0,'Gunther\'s Visage'),
(5666,2,0,'And thank you, $n.  Without your aid I may never have found my way to the Forsaken.',12,0,100,2,0,0,'Gunther\'s Visage'),
(5772,0,0,'Who dares to seek me out?!',14,8,100,15,0,0,'Lord Azrethoc\'s Image'),
(5772,1,0,'Insects!',14,8,100,0,0,0,'Lord Azrethoc\'s Image'),
(5772,2,0,'Come! Come to your deaths--if you dare!',14,8,100,396,0,0,'Lord Azrethoc\'s Image'),
(5773,0,0,'Pathetic Forsaken weakling. You wish to see my master? So be it.',12,1,100,25,0,0,'Jugkar Grim\'rod\'s Image'),
(5773,1,0,'Yes, come. My master and I shall be waiting.',12,1,100,273,0,0,'Jugkar Grim\'rod\'s Image'),
(6514,0,0,'%s pounds his chest, calling for help!',16,0,100,0,0,0,'Un\'Goro Gorilla'),
(6516,0,0,'%s looks tired. He then yawns and lies down next to A-Me 01',16,0,100,0,0,0,'Un\'Goro Thunderer'),
(6516,0,1,'%s snores loudly and cuddles up next to A-Me 01.',16,0,100,0,0,0,'Un\'Goro Thunderer'),
(7161,0,0,'Make sure to visit the Gizmotronic Apparatus to grab a lockpick and an E.C.A.C. You will definitely need both to complete your mission!',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Wrenix the Wretched'),
(7161,1,0,'%s points you to the Gizmotronic Apparatus.',16,0,100,0,0,0,'Wrenix the Wretched'),
(7166,0,0,'%s explodes, lighting the sky up in a brilliant fireworks display! It seems to be beckoning to you, rogue.',16,0,100,0,0,0,'Wrenix\'s Gizmotronic Apparatus'),
(7168,0,0,'What the squawk??? Squawk squawk, squawk? SQUAWK!',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Polly'),
(7917,0,0,'Greetings, $c!  Welcome to the Cathedral of Light!',12,0,100,3,0,0,'Brother Sarno'),
(8023,0,0,'%s chirps a goodbye to $n.',16,0,100,0,0,0,'Sharpbeak'),
(8380,0,0,'Stand Prepared! The naga won\'t wait long to press their advantage once they know we\'re alive.',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Captain Vanessa Beltis'),
(8390,0,0,'There! Job\'s done.',12,0,100,1,0,0,'Chemist Cuely'),
(8393,0,0,'Wha... what\'s happening?',12,0,100,15,0,0,'Thersa Windsong'),
(8480,0,0,'Glorious, indeed, Maltrake. It looks as if my plan worked perfectly. Wouldn\'t you say so, mortal?',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Kalaran the Deceiver'),
(8480,1,0,'%s lets loose a reptilian laugh... at least you think it\'s a laugh.',16,0,100,0,0,0,'Kalaran the Deceiver'),
(8480,2,0,'You would not have helped the legion of Blackrock had we just asked for your assistance, now would you?',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Kalaran the Deceiver'),
(8480,3,0,'SILENCE FOOL!',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Kalaran the Deceiver'),
(8480,4,0,'They will live, if only to see the fruits of their labor: the destruction and chaos that will surely ensue as the legion of Blackrock invade the gorge.',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Kalaran the Deceiver'),
(8480,5,0,'I leave you now, mortals. Alive and with these trinkets. Maltrake! Present them with the trinkets!',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Kalaran the Deceiver'),
(8480,6,0,'Oh yes, the molt - do not lose it. There are those of my kin in the Burning Steppes that would craft items that only the molt of the black Dragonflight could fortify.',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Kalaran the Deceiver'),
(8480,7,0,'%s begins to flap his massive wings faster. He is preparing for flight.',16,0,100,0,0,0,'Kalaran the Deceiver'),
(8480,8,0,'The legion of Blackrock comes, dwarflings! We shall scorch the earth and set fire to the heavens. None shall survive...',14,0,100,0,0,0,'Kalaran the Deceiver'),
(8509,0,0,'What will we do with them, master? They are of no use to us anymore.',12,0,100,6,0,0,'Squire Maltrake'),
(8509,1,0,'Right away, master!',12,0,100,2,0,0,'Squire Maltrake'),
(8581,0,0,'Who dares?! I will destroy you!',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Blood Elf Defender'),
(8581,1,0,'Mistress!! They seek to destroy your work!!',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Blood Elf Defender'),
(8581,2,0,'Ha! Now your death is ensured!',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Blood Elf Defender'),
(9119,0,0,'I hope this works!',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Muigin'),
(9119,1,0,'%s adds the haze to the Bloodpetal sprouts.',16,0,100,0,0,0,'Muigin'),
(9119,2,0,'Look at them go!',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Muigin'),
(9119,3,0,'%s laughs as he watches the pests run off.',16,0,100,11,0,0,'Muigin'),
(9298,0,0,'%s looks around nervously.',16,0,100,0,0,0,'Donova Snowden'),
(9298,1,0,'Are you sure you weren\'t followed here? I have a very bad feeling all of a sudden...',12,0,100,6,0,0,'Donova Snowden'),
(9298,2,0,'Be on your guard!',14,0,100,5,0,0,'Donova Snowden'),
(9298,3,0,'Please, follow me.',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Donova Snowden'),
(9298,4,0,'I haven\'t really figured out what it is, but there\'s something strange about the hot springs...',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Donova Snowden'),
(9298,5,0,'%s tosses the sword into the shallow pool.',16,0,100,61,0,0,'Donova Snowden'),
(9298,6,0,'I\'ve found that when I throw something into this water, it has improved incredibly when I retrieve it.',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Donova Snowden'),
(9298,7,0,'Well, whatever it is, it works quite well!',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Donova Snowden'),
(9298,8,0,'And I am determined to find out more... So if you need my help again, you know where I\'ll be.',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Donova Snowden'),
(9528,0,0,'Here is a beacon for you, $n.  You must keep it in your possession if you are to find the corrupted items we will need.',12,7,100,25,5000,0,'Arathandris Silversky - SAY_BEACON'),
(9529,0,0,'Here is a beacon for you, $n.  You must keep it in your possession if you are to find the corrupted items we will need.',12,1,100,25,5000,0,'Arathandris Silversky - SAY_BEACON'),
(9876,0,0,'Ach! Thank you so much, $n! I\'m free! Finally!',12,0,100,4,0,0,'Locheed'),
(9876,1,0,'You take care of yourself! I\'m gettin\' out o\' here.',12,0,100,5,0,0,'Locheed'),
(10667,0,0,'Let\'s find out the whole story.  That\'s going to take some magic...',12,0,100,1,0,0,'Chromie'),
(10667,1,0,'There, it is done.  The book has been enhanced...',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Chromie'),
(10926,0,0,'Daddy!',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Pamela1'),
(10926,1,0,'Daddy!  You\'re back!',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Pamela2'),
(10926,2,0,'Let\'s go play!  No, tell me a story, Daddy!  No... let\'s go pick flowers!  And play tea time!  I found my dollie, did I tell you?',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Pamela3'),
(10926,3,0,'I missed you so much, Daddy!',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Pamela4'),
(10936,0,0,'Pamela?  Are you there, honey?',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Joseph1'),
(10936,1,0,'I missed you too, honey.  And I\'m finally home...',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Joseph2'),
(10945,2,0,'Protect Davil Lightfire!',41,0,100,0,0,0,'Lightfire1'),
(11711,0,0,'Wait... did you hear that? Something approaches from the west!',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Sentinel Aynasha'),
(11711,1,0,'I\'ve run out of arrows! I\'m afraid if any more come you will need to take them on by yourself my friend.',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Sentinel Aynasha'),
(11711,2,0,'Praise Elune! I don\'t know if I could have survived the day without you, friend.',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Sentinel Aynasha'),
(11711,3,0,'My leg feels much better now, the remedy must be working. If you will excuse me, I must go report to my superiors about what has transpired here. ',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Sentinel Aynasha'),
(11711,4,0,'Please speak with Sentinel Onaeya at Maestra\'s Post in Ashenvale, she will see to it that you are properly rewarded for your bravery this day.',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Sentinel Aynasha'),
(11715,0,0,'$n, please take a look at the sample of the Vylestem vine that I took from the caverns, so that you know what to look for...',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Talendria'),
(12802,0,0,'%s becomes enraged!',16,0,100,0,0,0,'Rage Scar Yeti'),
(12803,0,0,'%s goes into a frenzy!',16,0,100,0,0,0,'Lord Lakmaeran'),
(14500,0,0,'Ah, here we are!  Well let\'s get to work, shall we...?',12,0,100,0,0,0,'J\'eevee'),
(14500,1,0,'Oh, right!  Over here now...',12,0,100,0,0,0,'J\'eevee'),
(14500,2,0,'And now... the final step!',12,0,100,0,0,0,'J\'eevee'),
(14500,3,0,'I\'m finished.  The parchment is made.  Now, return to Gorzeeki...',12,0,100,0,0,0,'J\'eevee'),
(14635,0,0,'Our pillas! Someone has stolen our pillas!',14,0,100,0,0,0,'Sleepy Dark Iron Worker to Player to Player'),
(14635,1,0,'We\'ll not let this act of madness go unpunished!',14,0,100,0,0,0,'Sleepy Dark Iron Worker to Player to Player'),
(14844,0,0,'Cheap beer!  Get your cheap beer right here!',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Sylannia'),
(14844,0,1,'Huzzah for the tipper!  Step right up and get your delicious, cold drinks right here!',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Sylannia'),
(14844,0,2,'Just in... another batch of Darkmoon Special Reserve.  Come get yours before they\'re all gone!',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Sylannia'),
(14844,0,3,'You there!  Yes you!  You look thirsty.  Get over here, I have just what you need!',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Sylannia'),
(14845,0,0,'Step right up!  Get your red hot wings right here!',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Stamp Thunderhorn'),
(14845,0,1,'Darkmoon Dogs fresh off the grill.  Come and get \'em while they\'re hot!',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Stamp Thunderhorn'),
(14845,0,2,'You\'ve got money and we\'ve got food.  What are you waiting for?!',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Stamp Thunderhorn'),
(14845,0,3,'For a limited time only, crunchy frog available exclusively here at the Darkmoon Faire.',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Stamp Thunderhorn'),
(15180,0,0,'%s shifts uncomfortably.',16,0,100,0,0,0,'Baristolth of the Shifting Sands'),
(15180,1,0,'When the time is right, my lady. All will be clear when the time is right. The master stirs even now. Look to the skies for the Brood of Nozdormu have returned.',12,0,100,1,0,0,'Baristolth of the Shifting Sands'),
(15183,0,0,'I will do my best to translate and describe what I see.',12,0,100,1,0,0,'Geologist Larksbane'),
(15183,1,0,'It is history... A history of Silithus... of Ahn\'Qiraj... of Titans and Old Gods... I read from the prophecy of C\'Thun as written by the Qiraji Prophet Skeram. A prophecy that portends a cataclysm... ',12,0,100,1,0,0,'Geologist Larksbane'),
(15183,2,0,'In the time before time, when the world was still in its infancy, a battle between a Titan and a being of unimaginable evil and power raged on this very soil. The prophecy is unclear about whether or not the Titan was vanquished in this battle but it illustrates that a Titan fell. An Old God had also fallen - or so it was thought. ',12,0,100,1,0,0,'Geologist Larksbane'),
(15183,3,0,'For millennia this being lay dormant beneath the world - biding its time. From its prison it waited for the exact moment at which to strike back at those that would see it harmed. ',12,0,100,1,0,0,'Geologist Larksbane'),
(15183,4,0,'The land of eternal starlight, Kalimdor, was a nurturing mother to all of its creatures. The magic of the Well of Eternity permeated the land and empowered the multitude of flora and fauna that would make the world their home. From this magical ether were born the silithid. It was through the silithid that the brooding Old God would reach and attempt to sunder the world that it once held in its unmerciful grasp.  ',12,0,100,1,0,0,'Geologist Larksbane'),
(15183,5,0,'The Old God would create avatars from the silithid in its own image. These avatars were to be known as Qiraji. Sentient and with purpose, the Qiraji would name their creator: C\'Thun was born... For many thousands of years the Qiraji worked feverishly to build a force capable of laying waste to the world that would betray their god. The great fortress city of Ahn\'Qiraj was created to house their growing armies and prepare for the coming of C\'Thun. ',12,0,100,1,0,0,'Geologist Larksbane'),
(15183,6,0,'This can\'t be right. An Old God could never be allowed to enter this world. The results would be... Oh dear!',12,0,100,5,0,0,'Geologist Larksbane'),
(15183,7,0,'%s regains her composure.',16,0,100,0,0,0,'Geologist Larksbane'),
(15183,8,0,'There is more.',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Geologist Larksbane'),
(15183,9,0,'The moment that C\'Thun had so patiently waited for had finally arrived. His children had spent thousands of years building an army capable of exacting revenge upon the whole of Kalimdor and now the prize was within their grasp. ',12,0,100,1,0,0,'Geologist Larksbane'),
(15183,10,0,'The Titans had long since vacated this world. Only the night elves that once inhabited this area were here to defend. Oh my! The next passage is fascinating! ',12,0,100,1,0,0,'Geologist Larksbane'),
(15183,11,0,'A mighty Qiraji known as General Rajaxx would command the initial incursion into Silithus. Only one would stand in his way: A night elf known as Staghelm. They refer to him as Khar\'sis or \'hand of the earth\' in the native Qiraji tongue. ',12,0,100,1,0,0,'Geologist Larksbane'),
(15183,12,0,'Staghelm and his armies were clearly overwhelmed as the endless flow of Rajaxx\'s troops poured into Silithus. It would seem as if Staghelm, however, was more than just a nuisance to the Qiraji. Under Staghelm, the whole of the night elf armies had come together to defend Kalimdor, greatly slowing the Qiraji forces. ',12,0,100,1,0,0,'Geologist Larksbane'),
(15183,13,0,'Unfortunately, the night elf defense was untenable and Rajaxx knew that they could not hold out much longer. Their tenacity, however, was causing great frustration to Rajaxx and causing even more frustration to his king. Wait, kings? Incredible... ',12,0,100,6,0,0,'Geologist Larksbane'),
(15183,14,0,'Vek\'nilash and Vek\'lor, known as the Twin Emperors of Ahn\'Qiraj, watched the war from the sanctuary of their temple. The clever brothers devised a plan to demoralize and divide Staghelm\'s forces.',12,0,100,1,0,0,'Geologist Larksbane'),
(15183,15,0,'Valstann Staghelm served as the right hand of Fandral. A proud and noble warrior, his dedication and adoration for his father unyielding... and the Twin Emperors sensed this as weakness. A weakness that could be exploited. ',12,0,100,1,0,0,'Geologist Larksbane'),
(15183,16,0,'The Qiraji forces were commanded to fall back and hide the bulk of their numbers beneath the sands of the desert. A small attack was ordered upon Southwind Village while the front lines of Staghelm\'s army were kept occupied.',12,0,100,1,0,0,'Geologist Larksbane'),
(15183,17,0,'Valstann, eager to please his father, convinced Fandral to allow him to take a small battalion to the defense of Southwind. Surely with the tide of battle turning their way, no harm could come to his beloved child. The trap was missed. Valstann was captured by the hiding Qiraji and Southwind Village obliterated. Rajaxx himself would take the captive Valstann to the front lines of the battle where - in front of Staghelm and the night elf forces - he would brutally execute the young night elf. ',12,0,100,1,0,0,'Geologist Larksbane'),
(15183,18,0,'The war continued but the will of the great leader was sapped. The whole of Silithus was soon engulfed by the silithid and their Qiraji hosts.',12,0,100,1,0,0,'Geologist Larksbane'),
(15183,19,0,'Poor man, this explains so much.',12,0,100,6,0,0,'Geologist Larksbane'),
(15183,20,0,'The night elf army was pushed back through Un\'Goro, to the borders of the Tanaris desert. Something in Un\'Goro prevented the Qiraji from being able to take the land. I do not quite understand this word but I believe it to mean \'God Lands.\' It is stated that they could not \'take the God Lands.\'  ',12,0,100,1,0,0,'Geologist Larksbane'),
(15183,21,0,'Fascinating, this coincides with theories of Un\'Goro being the home of the Titans when they inhabited Kalimdor. Perhaps Aman\'thul himself watched over \'The God Lands.\'',12,0,100,273,0,0,'Geologist Larksbane'),
(15183,22,0,'Hrm, curious... This ends abruptly. In Tanaris the Qiraji document facing a bronze dragon. There is much missing from this... More information must be found! Surely they are planning to invade Kalimdor once more! ',12,0,100,6,0,0,'Geologist Larksbane'),
(15362,0,0,'The walls of the chamber tremble. Something is happening...',42,0,100,0,0,0,'Malfurion Stormrage'),
(15362,1,0,'Be steadfast, champion. I know why it is that you are here and I know what it is that you seek. Eranikus will not give up the shard freely. He has been twisted... twisted by the same force that you seek to destroy.',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Malfurion Stormrage'),
(15362,2,0,'Are you really surprised? Is it hard to believe that the power of an Old God could reach even inside the Dream? It is true - Eranikus, Tyrant of the Dream, wages a battle against us all. The Nightmare follows in his wake of destruction.',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Malfurion Stormrage'),
(15362,3,0,'Understand this, Eranikus wants nothing more than to be brought to Azeroth from the Dream. Once he is out, he will stop at nothing to destroy my physical manifestation. This, however, is the only way in which you could recover the scepter shard.',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Malfurion Stormrage'),
(15362,4,0,'You will bring him back into this world, champion.',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Malfurion Stormrage'),
(15362,5,0,'%s bows.',16,0,100,2,0,0,'Malfurion Stormrage'),
(15440,0,0,'Aye, lads!  Things are about to get quite ugly.',14,0,100,5,0,0,'Captain Blackanvil');
INSERT IGNORE INTO `creature_text` (`entry`,`groupid`,`id`,`text`,`type`,`language`,`probability`,`emote`,`duration`,`sound`,`comment`) VALUES
(15440,1,0,'Looks like it\'s going to be one of those days.',14,0,100,0,0,0,'Captain Blackanvil'),
(15440,2,0,'I should\'ve grabbed a bigger sword.',14,0,100,0,0,0,'Captain Blackanvil'),
(15440,3,0,'Footmen, make a line!',14,0,100,25,0,0,'Captain Blackanvil'),
(15441,2,0,'Captain!  Lieutenant Stouthammer requests your presence!  The enemy is approaching, sir!',12,0,100,66,0,0,'Ironforge Brigade Rifleman'),
(16114,0,0,'Your message did reach us, Commander, but by no means is our involvement here sanctioned by the Grand Crusader.',12,0,100,1,0,0,'Scarlet Commander Marjhan'),
(16114,1,0,'The heathens will be forced to react. Orcs, bull-men...',12,0,100,1,0,0,'Scarlet Commander Marjhan'),
(16114,2,0,'Whatever. The revolting, unkempt Horde filth...',12,0,100,5,0,0,'Scarlet Commander Marjhan'),
(16114,3,0,'Too little, too late. The dam has broken. We are a bump in the road at best.',12,0,100,274,0,0,'Scarlet Commander Marjhan'),
(16114,4,0,'There is always... Ashbringer.',12,0,100,1,0,0,'Scarlet Commander Marjhan'),
(16115,0,0,'Your leader takes residence at the doorstep to Naxxramas. Do you think he does not feel the pressure? ',12,0,100,6,0,0,'Commander Eligor Dawnbringer'),
(16115,1,0,'%s lowers the sound of his voice to a whisper.',16,0,100,0,0,0,'Commander Eligor Dawnbringer'),
(16115,2,0,'Even demons are capable of fear...',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Commander Eligor Dawnbringer'),
(16115,3,0,'Scourge activity in the Plaguelands has increased ten-fold. We are receiving reports of Scourge attacks from as far away as Kalimdor! Now how do you suppose this has happened? How have the wretched undead done that which was previously thought impossible? Is nowhere safe?',12,0,100,1,0,0,'Commander Eligor Dawnbringer'),
(16115,4,0,'Tauren.',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Commander Eligor Dawnbringer'),
(16115,5,0,'You lack tact, Commander. This is not surprising. However, you are right in that the Horde will be forced to act. But not just the Horde. They already come - heroes from across the world.',12,0,100,1,0,0,'Commander Eligor Dawnbringer'),
(16115,6,0,'So why are you here? What are we to do if there is no hope?',12,0,100,6,0,0,'Commander Eligor Dawnbringer'),
(16115,7,0,'So this is what you have come for? To try and claim that which is the reason for the Dawn\'s existence and the Crusade\'s downfall? You open old wounds with your words, Commander!',12,0,100,6,0,0,'Commander Eligor Dawnbringer'),
(16115,8,0,'The Ashbringer is dead and there will never be another like him. The lesser Mograine is a far cry from the man his father was. You know this, Commander! It was, after all, your own leadership that was responsible for the death of the Scarlet Highlord Mograine.',12,0,100,5,0,0,'Commander Eligor Dawnbringer'),
(16115,9,0,'It was your leadership that manipulated a grieving child to try and recover the sword. A child that has grown into a man with nothing but vengeance and hatred in his heart! And for what? You are no closer to the sword now than you were five years ago. ',12,0,100,25,0,0,'Commander Eligor Dawnbringer'),
(16115,10,0,'Yet you think that recovering Ashbringer will somehow turn the tide of battle? Let me let you in on a little secret, Commander: The power of the Ashbringer came from the man who would wield it... I was there, Commander. I watched him burn legions of undead in righteous fire before he would even unsheathe the blade. Alas, your grasp on history is ... lacking.',12,0,100,1,0,0,'Commander Eligor Dawnbringer'),
(16115,11,0,'Now be silent and note where you are, lest I inform Lord Fordring and his knights that you are no longer here on amicable terms. I am certain he would take great pleasure in seeing to your \'atonement.\'',12,0,100,5,0,0,'Commander Eligor Dawnbringer'),
(16134,0,0,'Watch, druid. The earth still breathes. It yearns to be cleansed.',12,0,100,1,0,0,'Rimblat Earthshatter'),
(16135,0,0,'That is wonderous, Rimblat! Even this foul, sundered earth is not beyond healing.',12,0,100,273,0,0,'Rayne'),
(17207,0,0,'Who challenges Naias? Puny $r, you are little better than those mindless trolls I have played against each other like so many pieces on a game board!',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Naias'),
(17238,3,0,'It must be the purity of the Mark of the Lightbringer that is drawing forth the Scourge to us.  We must proceed with caution lest we be overwhelmed!',12,7,100,1,0,0,'Q Tomb of the Lighbringer'),
(17238,4,0,'We are beset upon again!  Defend yourself!',12,7,100,5,0,0,'Q Tomb of the Lighbringer'),
(17238,5,0,'This land truly needs to be cleansed by the Light!  Let us continue on to the tomb.  It isn\'t far now.',12,7,100,1,0,0,'Q Tomb of the Lighbringer'),
(17238,6,0,'Very well, let us continue.',12,7,100,1,0,0,'Q Tomb of the Lighbringer'),
(17238,7,0,'Thank you my friend for making this possible.  This is a day that I shall never forget!  I think I will stay a while.  Please return to High Priestess MacDonnell at the camp.  I know that she\'ll be keenly interested to know of what has transpired here.',12,7,100,2,0,0,'Q Tomb of the Lighbringer'),
(17663,0,0,'If only I could get back to the mushroom thicket. I have not seen such a mature cluster in my lifetime!',12,7,100,0,0,0,'Jessera of Mac\'Aree'),
(18528,0,0,'%s falls silent and a quiet tension falls over the nearby Sha\'tar forces as Xi\'ri makes his decision.',16,0,100,0,0,0,'Xiri'),
(18528,1,0,'%s begins channelling the powers of the Light.',16,0,100,0,0,0,'Xiri'),
(19294,0,0,'Up here on the hill, $n.',15,0,100,0,0,0,'Earthbinder Galandria Nightbreeze'),
(19294,1,0,'I have an idea.  Let\'s plant this shard in the ground and see what happens.',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Earthbinder Galandria Nightbreeze'),
(19294,2,0,'The evil emanating from the crystal shard has lured one of the colossi.  Put it down quick!',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Earthbinder Galandria Nightbreeze'),
(22862,0,0,'Come closer, demon! Death awaits!',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Caalen'),
(22862,0,1,'Illidan\'s lapdogs! Destroy them all!',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Caalen'),
(22862,0,2,'I\'ve a message for your master, scum!',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Caalen'),
(22862,0,3,'Pathetic worm... your master\'s days are over!',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Caalen'),
(22862,0,4,'For Xi\'ri!  For the Sha\'tar!',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Caalen'),
(22862,0,5,'Your end is at hand, Illidari!',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Caalen'),
(22864,0,0,'Onward, Scryers!  Show Illidan\'s lackeys the temper of our steel!',14,0,100,0,0,0,'Fyra Downstar'),
(23712,0,0,'What\'s happening?',12,7,100,18,0,0,'Touring Orphan'),
(23712,0,1,'I want to go back to the orphanage!',12,7,100,18,0,0,'Touring Orphan'),
(23712,0,2,'Matron!  Is that bad man going to eat us?',12,7,100,18,0,0,'Touring Orphan'),
(23712,0,3,'If my dad were alive, he would put out the fires!',12,7,100,18,0,0,'Touring Orphan'),
(23712,0,4,'If my mom were alive, she would put out the fires!',12,7,100,18,0,0,'Touring Orphan'),
(23941,0,0,'I surrender! Stay your blade!',12,0,100,5,0,0,'Gavis Greyshield'),
(23941,1,0,'I will go with you. Just spare my men. They\'re good lads who\'ve only made a mistake...',12,0,100,1,0,0,'Gavis Greyshield'),
(25335,0,0,'$n is going to join us on our assault. Let us bring peace to my ancestors!',12,1,100,396,0,0,'Longrunner Proudhoof'),
(25335,1,0,'WE STRIKE!',14,1,100,15,0,0,'Longrunner Proudhoof'),
(25335,2,0,'An ambush. Return them to their rest!',12,1,100,5,0,0,'Longrunner Proudhoof'),
(25335,3,0,'Regain your strength. The place where Steeljaw was felled is just ahead.',12,1,100,396,0,0,'Longrunner Proudhoof'),
(25335,4,0,'There\'s the dog\'s banner and there\'s his corpse. What\'s that? He\'s upon us!',12,1,100,25,0,0,'Longrunner Proudhoof'),
(25335,5,0,'You fought well. Now go north to your orc outpost and inform Overlord Bor\'gorok of our success!',12,1,100,113,0,0,'Longrunner Proudhoof'),
(25759,0,0,'Thank you, $r. I will take this miserable cur from you now.',12,1,100,1,0,0,'Valiance Keep Officer'),
(28897,0,0,'So hungry...',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Scarlet Ghoul'),
(28897,0,1,'Must feed...',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Scarlet Ghoul'),
(28897,0,2,'Smell flesh... close...',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Scarlet Ghoul'),
(35589,0,0,'The Argent Crusade invites you to test your skills in honorable combat against other heroes of Azeroth at the Argent Tournament.',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Jaeren Sunsworn'),
(35589,1,0,'The champions of the world\'s great nations have gathered at the Argent Tournament Grounds in northeastern Icecrown to face all challengers.',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Jaeren Sunsworn'),
(35604,0,0,'The Argent Crusade invites you to test your skills in honorable combat against other heroes of Azeroth at the Argent Tournament.',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Arelas Brightstar'),
(35604,1,0,'The champions of the world\'s great nations have gathered at the Argent Tournament Grounds in northeastern Icecrown to face all challengers.',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Arelas Brightstar'),
(40253,0,0,'Warriors of de Darkspear Tribe, our leader, de great Vol\'jin prepares to reclaim de Echo Isles.',12,0,100,1,0,0,'Champion Uru\'zin'),
(40253,1,0,'De battle ahead will be de true test of de warrior\'s skill, de true test of loyalty.',12,0,100,1,0,0,'Champion Uru\'zin'),
(40253,2,0,'De spirits of our ancestors will be watchin\' us and aidin\' us in dis battle.',12,0,100,1,0,0,'Champion Uru\'zin'),
(40253,3,0,'Do dem proud! Show dem your bravery and your ferocity! Bring honor to their spirits!',12,0,100,25,0,0,'Champion Uru\'zin'),
(40253,4,0,'An\' most of all, we be showin\' Zalazane dat his time be at an end! Dat he will give back what be rightfully ours!',12,0,100,5,0,0,'Champion Uru\'zin');
